# The api/ folder ships the serverless functions (data / feed / login / logout /
# warm + the _core, _auth and _payload helpers), so it must NOT be ignored
# wholesale. Only the secret is excluded — on Vercel the Apollo key comes from
# the APOLLO_SWIMM_KEY env var.
api/swimm_key.txt
swimm_key.txt
.env
.env.*
.vercel/

# NEVER deploy the raw payload. Anything at the project root is served as a
# public static file, so shipping this would hand every call, contact and note
# to anyone who guessed the URL — no login required. The deployed copy lives in
# api/_payload.py, which is inside the functions directory and is only readable
# through /api/feed (session cookie required).
swimm-payload.json

# Local tooling — no reason to expose it, and make_users.py is the password tool.
# Anything left at the project root is served as a public static file, so this
# list is a security boundary, not tidiness: a script that lands here is
# readable by anyone who guesses its name.
make_users.py
verify_lockdown.py
check_payload.py
check_login.py
build_swimm.py
meetings.py
diagnose_calls.py
probe_dispositions.py
probe_recordings.py
match_outcomes.py
analyze_outcomes.py

__pycache__/
api/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
README.md

# generated by make_users.py — passwords and env secrets
swimm-logins.txt
swimm-vercel-env.txt
swimm-users-current.txt

.github/
.gitignore
